---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
  title="About Niyora"
  description="Who is behind Niyora, why it exists, and what it will and won't do with your data."
  ogImage="https://assets.niyora.com/niyora-launch-poster.jpg"
  canonicalUrl="https://niyora.com/about/"
>
  <section class="s left">
    <div class="about">
      <h1>About Niyora</h1>

      <p class="lead">
        Niyora is an app for the days before your period, when your feelings get
        louder than usual. It is built by one person, in Norway, and it is early.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is behind it</h2>
      <img src="/neha.jpg" alt="Neha Prasad" class="photo" loading="lazy" />
      <p>
        I'm Neha Prasad. I'm a doctor and a product designer, and I've spent ten
        years working in health. I went looking for a way through PMS that didn't
        ask me to change my body, started where I trust, the research, and built
        what I wanted to use myself.
      </p>

      <h2>Why it exists</h2>
      <p>
        Most of what's offered for PMS either medicates it or tracks it and stops
        there. Niyora predicts your week too. The difference is what happens next:
        it helps you in the actual hard hour, where almost nothing else does.
      </p>
      <p>
        The quieter, stronger thread in the research is emotion regulation.
        Naming what you feel, settling your body, and seeing the thought from a
        step back. No hormones to take, no device to wear, no data to hand over.
        Everything in the app is one small rep of that, done in about a minute.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="inline" href="/research/">The research Niyora is built on</a> is
        published, with the sources graded.
      </p>

      <h2>What it will not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No ads, no profile, no data sold.</li>
        <li>No account needed. Your period dates stay on your device.</li>
        <li>
          Before your words go to Moon's AI, names and identifying details are
          stripped on your phone. What is left can't point back to you.
        </li>
        <li>
          It is not a diagnosis, a therapist, or crisis care. If you're in danger,
          contact your local emergency number.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The long version lives in <a class="inline" href="/privacy/">the privacy page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Where it is now</h2>
      <p>
        Niyora is in testing, not on the App Store yet.
        <a class="inline" href="/changelog/">What's new</a> tracks what ships.
        <a class="inline" href="/talk/">Say hello</a> if you want to shape it, or
        tell us you're interested and we'll keep building.
      </p>

      <div class="links">
        <a class="link" href="/talk/">Say hello</a>
        <a class="link" href="/#interest">I'm interested</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>

<style>
  /* Narrow reading column for the long-form about copy. */
  .about { max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78); }
  .about h2 { margin: 40px 0 14px; }
  .about p, .about li {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .about ul { padding-left: 20px; }
  .about li { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .photo {
    width: 96px;
    height: 96px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  a.inline {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.25);
  }
  a.inline:hover { border-color: rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.8); }
  .links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
  .link {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 10px 18px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
    font-size: 13px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.18s ease, border-color 0.18s ease, transform 0.18s ease;
  }
  .link:hover {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.36);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
</style>
